.TH TK 1 "2026-10-02" "sc-fleet 0.1.0" "sc-fleet manual"
.SH NAME
tk \- the task board, from a shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBtk\fR [\fBls\fR] [\fB-a\fR] [\fB--section\fR \fIS\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
\fBtk new\fR \fItext\fR [\fB--due\fR \fID\fR] [\fB--sched\fR \fID\fR] [\fB--every\fR \fIRULE\fR] [\fB--priority\fR \fIP\fR] [\fB--section\fR \fIS\fR]
\fBtk start\fR \fImatch\fR
\fBtk done\fR \fImatch\fR
\fBtk cancel\fR \fImatch\fR
\fBtk defer\fR \fImatch\fR \fIdate\fR
\fBtk move\fR \fImatch\fR \fB--to\fR \fISECTION\fR [\fB--create\fR]
\fBtk prune\fR [\fB--keep-days\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--dry-run\fR]
\fBtk doctor\fR
\fBtk path\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The board is one Markdown file in the Obsidian Tasks emoji grammar. Until now
it was reachable two ways: an agent's slash command, which needs an agent
session, and \fBtasks.py\fR, which does not look or behave like anything else
in the fleet.
.PP
\fBtk\fR is the fleet surface over that engine. It adds the identity, the
band on state changes and the spine verb names, and it adds nothing else.
Every flag is handed to the engine untouched, so anything \fBtk\fR cannot
spell the engine still can, and \fB--line\fR \fIN\fR keeps working when a
match is ambiguous.
.SH WHY A WRAPPER AND NOT A REWRITE
The engine owns the grammar, the recurrence maths and the section routing,
and it has a test suite. Reimplementing any of that in bash to make it look
like a fleet tool would trade correctness for cosmetics. The wrapper is
roughly a hundred lines and holds no task logic at all.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBls\fR, \fBlist\fR
Surfaced tasks: open or in progress, and due today, overdue, or past their
scheduled date. \fB-a\fR shows
the whole board, section by section, with line numbers for \fB--line\fR.
This is what bare \fBtk\fR runs.
.TP
\fBnew\fR, \fBadd\fR
Add a task, to \fB## Inbox\fR unless \fB--section\fR names another; choosing
the section is the caller's job.
.TP
\fBstart\fR, \fBdone\fR, \fBcancel\fR, \fBdefer\fR, \fBmove\fR
State changes, each matched by a substring of the task text. \fBdone\fR
spawns the next occurrence of a recurring task; \fBcancel\fR ends the chain.
.TP
\fBprune\fR
Archive finished tasks older than \fB--keep-days\fR. \fB--dry-run\fR changes
nothing and therefore prints no band.
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR, \fBcheck\fR
Validate the file: malformed dates, broken recurrence chains, duplicate
entries. Read-only.
.TP
\fBpath\fR
Print the board's path, for piping into an editor or a grep.
.SH VERB NAMES
\fBnew\fR and \fBdoctor\fR are the fleet spine's names for what the engine
calls \fBadd\fR and \fBcheck\fR. Both spellings are accepted, because the
engine's are already in muscle memory and breaking them buys nothing.
.SH ART
Bare \fBtk\fR lists rather than drawing a splash, because it is the thing you
type thirty times a day. The splash is on \fB--help\fR. Only state-changing
verbs print a band, and the band prints after the engine has succeeded, so it
never claims something that was refused.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBTK_STORE\fR
Directory holding the board; the file is \fItasks.md\fR inside it.
Overrides the config key \fBtk.store\fR, which defaults to the \fBnotes\fR
key, which defaults to \fI~/notes\fR (\fI~/.config/sc-fleet/config\fR; see
\fBsc config\fR).
.TP
\fBTK_ART\fR, \fBTK_NO_ART\fR, \fBSC_ART\fR, \fBSC_NO_ART\fR, \fBNO_COLOR\fR
Art and colour overrides. The most specific setting wins and, at the same
level, off beats on.
.TP
\fBTK_TRACE\fR
Set to anything for \fBset -x\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI<store>/tasks.md\fR
The board.
.TP
\fIlib/tasks.py\fR
The engine, in the sc-fleet checkout. \fBtk\fR refuses if it is absent.
The grammar it implements is \fIdocs/tasks.md\fR.
.TP
\fIlib/sckit.sh\fR
The fleet kit. Optional: without it \fBtk\fR runs with plain output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. 1 on a refusal, including an unknown subcommand and a match
that finds no open task. 2 when a match is ambiguous; \fB--line\fR \fIN\fR
picks one.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tk                              what is due
tk -a                           the whole board with line numbers
tk new "chase the 14 Sep capture hole" --due 2026-09-22 --priority high
tk start "capture hole"
tk done  "capture hole"
tk defer "EOY expense" 2027-02-01
tk move  "model_eval phase 3" --to Backlog
tk doctor
nvim "$(tk path)"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
